SUMMARY:Conn Peak at Lake Hennessey
DESCRIPTION:Go Wild Hikers Have Moved to Heylo.com\nIt's time for another 
 trip to Lake Hennessey. We'll hike up to Conn Peak overlooking the lake. A
 t the top there's a picnic table and a cool stone labyrinth. Moore Creek P
 ark is 1\,600 acres of rugged terrain including Oak woodlands\, Douglas Fi
 r & Madrone forest\, grasslands\, and chaparral. Wildlife in the park is p
 lentiful\, including large mammals such as black bears\, mountain lions\, 
 bobcat\, gray fox and coyote. Best for individuals with at least a moderat
 e level of fitness.\n\n**Important information**\nIf you've enjoyed hiking
  with this group\, follow me as I move Go Wild Hikers to a new platform by
  the end of May called Heylo.com\n\nIt's people like you that have made th
 is group so great!! Thank you all for being members of Go Wild Hikers and 
 I appreciate the large number of Hikers who have already followed the grou
 p to Heylo. The Shiloh Hike on Sunday May 31 still has some room.\n**Upcom
 ing events for Go Wild Hikers in June will include Hood Mtn\, Taylor Mtn\,
  Annadel and North Sonoma Mtn to Jack London.**\n[https://heylo.com/invite
 /PpURbZWX](http://clicks.meetup.com/ls/click?upn=u001.NY3oBFzZ5LJDG7YcnfSA
 KgvWkdmOX3k5-2FX9Cwzxfa6ZYDGAbpDzbtJiez6KtS8H-2Fj8h8_7Hv-2FAQY7Bu3bAT0Za4b
