 d0MfRDgce5PKC7X-2Fe-2BAtfcJ65iiVCOF3c8xjt9kUPDuF2i5DJph2HIjpYgSc5Y68b-2Fvb
 YJnf-2BugAgZrpaf4-2FAZTH7CUV1Vy7YxpcRfleHGUzyovaTRnjha29jbqUlXWFkk-2BTFCsf
 aetu4-2FLp8RX1EkXlszzHYJgjKC0Wj0L4g9-2BM-2FBrlew7aw9m6nTRse0ZnQqkOF-2FmXiy
 zA7UY7RLs5DXHegozj1Cn2gBVIqUcyF01GGur-2FpsbuaIxAEj-2FxkCPXl-2FDAXz4GZR2dqm
 J2pEwYb7FwrkUj3K4MHU3Jv1T0uHrMgu2Gtcjy1oWuAj9a0P1fOZ6MgnlNfXzTB8vlnwzQATLA
 GEGaZ6tTOsjPnnXYQ6c6qZTlgf4L4J3HYa-2BjVkmLJjtyD3FlKBISyaxvg84yV4xubj7p97uQ
 1s4qepMweZdnzHrp77I8YLFrMx4hp83o-3D)\n\nClick on the link above to join fo
 r free. It just takes a few clicks to create your profile.\nHappy trails\,
  this is not the end but the beginning of a different trail for Go Wild Hi
 kers. Come and Hike with us. Zoli\nBack to the current Hike.\n\n**Where We
  Meet/Important Directions**\nMoore Creek Park\n2602 Chiles Pope Valley Rd
 \, St Helena\, CA 94574\n**Carpool if you can - This is a very Popular Par
 k!**\nSouth on Hwy 128 past Calistoga - Left on Deer Park Rd (Sign Pacific
  Union College) - Right on Silverado Trail - Left on Sage Valley Rd/Hwy 12
 8 - Past Lake Hennessey - Pay Attention - Left on Chiles Pope Valley Rd - 
 Left into Moore Creek Park past a private house on a very narrow road ther
 e is a large parking lot.\nGive yourself plenty of time to arrive. It's of
 ten farther than you think.\n\n**The Hike (Group Hike #344)**\nChiles Cree
 k\, Whiskey Ridge\, Conn Peak and Shoreline trails\, - a lollipop hike\nAl
 lTrails Map -\nhttps://www.alltrails.com/explore/recording/lake-hennessey-
 e70981f\nDistance - 6 miles/9.7 kilometers\nElevation change - 900 feet/27
 4 meters\nDifficulty - 6+ out of 10 - Moderate\nExposures - 30% sun/70 % s
 hade - creek crossing\, poison oak\, ticks/insects.\nBring plenty of water
 . At least 68 oz./2 liters.\nDogs - Yes\, friendly dogs on a leash are per
 mitted at Lake Hennessey section (this hike). But they're prohibited in Mo
 ore Creek (different hike).\nFacilities at trail head - Port O Potti\nCost
  - Suggested $5 cash donation. No one turned away!\nParking - Free - Napa 
 Ag & Open Space welcomes donations.\nRemember to wear appropriate hiking s
 hoes\, bring plenty of water for your dog too\, a hat\, a snack/lunch and 
 layered clothing.\nPlease Do Not Use Any scented products the day of a gro
 up hike!\nOf course we will all look out for each other but ultimately\, h
 ikers are responsible for their own safety and well-being during hikes.\n\
 n**After Hike Gathering?**\nThe Calistoga Creamery\n1473 Lincoln Avenue\, 
 Calistoga 94515\nCome to the Calistoga Creamery to enjoy organic ice cream
  and organic frozen yogurt\, thick custom milk shakes\, root beer floats a
 nd sundaes. No high fructose corn syrup\, artificial colors or flavors. No
  hydrogenated oils and no GMOS.\n\n**When We Meet**\nSaturday May 23\, 202
 6\n8:30 am - 12:00 pm\n**Carpool if you can - This is a very Popular Park!
 **\nIf your plans change after you sign up even if you're on the waitlist\
 , please update your RSVP.\nDo Not Attend if you are sick\, running a feve
 r\, were exposed to or have tested positive for Covid-19 or any other cont
 agion!\nHike may be changed\, rescheduled or cancelled in case of excessiv
 e heat\, rain\, smoke/AQI\, illness\, zombie apocalypse etc... Check your 
 email the night before for any possible changes.
